epth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":14,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All 6 tests now pass. I also checked the edge cases in the docstrings: `-$0.05`, `-$1,234.56`, `0.5` → 50, and ties broken by name.\n\nBugs fixed:\n\n1. **`ledger/money.py` `format_cents`**: negative amounts came out wrong. Python's `//` and `%` round toward negative infinity, so -310 became `-$-4.90` instead of `-$3.10`. It now does the division on the absolute value and adds the sign afterwards.\n2. **`ledger/parse.py` `parse_date`**: month and day were swapped in the result. It now returns `(year, month, day)`. This was also the only reason `parse_record` failed.\n3. **`ledger/report.py` `top_items`**: items were sorted by total from smallest to largest, and ties had no defined order. It now sorts by total from largest to smallest, with ties ordered by item name A–Z. This also fixed `summary_line`.","ttft_ms":3059,"type":"result","duration_ms":41851,"uuid":"b379be75-4a04-43b9-9449-e979196cec67","ttft_stream_ms":1342,"time_to_request_ms":23,"first_content_frame_ms":1342,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
